pan/bi: restore the forced-TLS access hint on register-allocator spills

Thread-local storage on Valhall is per-thread scratch space that the register
allocator spills to and refills from. Those accesses must carry the hardware
"force" memory-access hint (Mali's "force access in discarded threads"): a
thread that has already been killed by a discard/demote can still be the one
another thread's spilled value is read back from, so the load/store has to
happen regardless of the thread's liveness.

Commit 43ffcf06 ("pan/bi,nir: Divide memory_access from segments") moved the
hint out of the segment encoding into a per-instruction field. The NIR
load/store path sets it (bi_emit_load/bi_emit_store), but the register
allocator builds its spill stores and refill loads through bi_store_tl() and
bi_load_tl() and left the new field at zero. Those instructions are then
emitted as plain global accesses, so spilled values can be read as garbage
when the spilling thread's liveness and the reloading thread's differ.

Under DXVK this shows up as wrong colour output from shaders that spill: the
register allocator spills large D3D-generated pixel shaders aggressively
(Unity's lighting/exposure/post-processing shaders among them), and a bad
refill produces NaN/Inf that tonemaps to white and is then held by the
temporal exposure/TAA history, so the whole frame stays white.

Restore the hint on both helpers.

Ported from upstream Mesa 33e67876 ("pan/bi: Restore VA_MEMORY_ACCESS_FORCE
for spills and refills"), which is not in the pinned Mesa tree.

diff --git a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_ra.c b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_ra.c
--- a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_ra.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_ra.c
@@ -728,26 +728,31 @@ bi_tls_ptr(bool hi)
 bi_instr *
 bi_load_tl(bi_builder *b, unsigned bits, bi_index dst, unsigned offset)
 {
+   bi_instr *I;
    if (b->shader->arch >= 9) {
       assert(offset < 0x8000);  /* valhall has 16 bit signed offset */
-      return bi_load_to(b, bits, dst, bi_tls_ptr(false), bi_tls_ptr(true),
-                        BI_SEG_TL, offset);
+      I = bi_load_to(b, bits, dst, bi_tls_ptr(false), bi_tls_ptr(true),
+                     BI_SEG_TL, offset);
    } else {
-      return bi_load_to(b, bits, dst, bi_imm_u32(offset), bi_zero(), BI_SEG_TL,
-                        0);
+      I = bi_load_to(b, bits, dst, bi_imm_u32(offset), bi_zero(), BI_SEG_TL, 0);
    }
+   I->mem_access = VA_MEMORY_ACCESS_FORCE;
+
+   return I;
 }

 void
 bi_store_tl(bi_builder *b, unsigned bits, bi_index src, unsigned offset)
 {
+   bi_instr *I;
    if (b->shader->arch >= 9) {
       assert(offset < 0x8000);  /* valhall has 16 bit signed offset */
-      bi_store(b, bits, src, bi_tls_ptr(false), bi_tls_ptr(true), BI_SEG_TL,
-               offset);
+      I = bi_store(b, bits, src, bi_tls_ptr(false), bi_tls_ptr(true), BI_SEG_TL,
+                   offset);
    } else {
-      bi_store(b, bits, src, bi_imm_u32(offset), bi_zero(), BI_SEG_TL, 0);
+      I = bi_store(b, bits, src, bi_imm_u32(offset), bi_zero(), BI_SEG_TL, 0);
    }
+   I->mem_access = VA_MEMORY_ACCESS_FORCE;
 }

 static void
